	<h1>Getting started</h1>
	<norn-rich-text>
		<p>Install the project, then run it once to see it work. The steps below take a few minutes on a new machine.</p>
		<norn-heading-anchor @slug="install">Install</norn-heading-anchor>
		<p>The package needs Node 24 or later. Check the version with <code>node --version</code> first.</p>
		<p>Add the package to the project as a development dependency, so it stays out of the production install.</p>
		<norn-heading-anchor @slug="with-npm" :@level="3">With npm</norn-heading-anchor>
		<p>Run <code>npm install --save-dev @example/core</code> in the project folder. npm writes the version to the lockfile.</p>
		<p>Commit the lockfile with the change, so every machine installs the same version.</p>
		<norn-heading-anchor @slug="usage">Usage</norn-heading-anchor>
		<p>Import <code>greet</code> from the package and call it with a name. It returns the greeting as a string.</p>
		<p>Pass a second argument to change the greeting, such as <code>"Good morning"</code> in place of <code>"hello"</code>.</p>
		<p>Call it as often as needed: it keeps no state between calls.</p>
	</norn-rich-text>
</norn-sidebar-layout>
